 "checks": "Every table's cells sum to its printed totals, and the per-mouse totals sum to the pooled Extended Data Fig. 6c (667 and 290 mutations, 77 and 172 clones, 45,336 and 102,357 bp). Frequencies from the tables reproduce Fig. 2d. Most clones are counted at a fixed 596 bp. Every printed P value in Fig. 2c-f reproduces from the source data with the stated two-tailed unpaired Student's t-test. The text's 'approximately fourfold' reduction is 5.2-fold for J_H4 and 3.8-fold for Bcl6 in the source data. The chromatograms of the published mice are not in the lab's sequencing download (see the Genesifter catalogue), so the study cannot be re-run from traces."
